; Control code 0: print a name phrase passed on the stack
;
; The caller of the message printer pushed the address of a name phrase (as
; returned by #R$71E2, 0 for none) below its return address. This takes it off
; the stack, closing the gap, clears the article flag ($B703) and, if it is not
; 0, prints the name with #R$7434.
; .
; The printer calls this handler with IX at the code byte. Return Z when there
; is nothing to print; NZ with a word token in DE and the printer prints it.
;
; O:A 0 (nothing more to print)
; O:F Z
@label=PrintStackedName
c$7367 XOR A         ;
 $7368 LD ($B703),A  ; PhraseMode: no article
 $736B POP DE        ;
 $736C POP HL        ;
 $736D EX (SP),HL    ;
 $736E PUSH DE       ;
 $736F LD A,H        ;
 $7370 OR L          ;
 $7371 CALL NZ,$7434 ;
 $7374 XOR A         ;
 $7375 RET           ;
